---
import MarketingLayout from '../layouts/MarketingLayout.astro';
import CopyBox from '../components/CopyBox.astro';
import { site } from '../config/site';
import installPrompt from '../data/generated/install-prompt.txt?raw';
---

<MarketingLayout
	title="Install"
	description="Install pohunek with the coding agent you already use, or by hand on Linux x86_64 and macOS on Apple Silicon."
>
	<section class="container">
		<header class="page-hero">
			<span class="eyebrow">Install</span>
			<h1>Install with your agent</h1>
			<p class="lead">
				The easiest route is to let the agent you already use do the setup. Paste the prompt into Claude Code, Codex or
				another agent with shell access on the machine that should host sessions. It asks for approval before it installs
				the login service or any runtime hook.
			</p>
		</header>
	</section>

	<section class="container section">
		<CopyBox title="install prompt" text={installPrompt.trimEnd()} />
		<p class="muted note">Repeat it on every machine that should host sessions. Remote hosts must join the same NetBird network.</p>
	</section>

	<section class="container section">
		<div class="section-head">
			<span class="eyebrow">Manual</span>
			<h2>Install by hand</h2>
		</div>
		<div class="grid cols-2">
			<article class="card">
				<h3>Linux x86_64</h3>
				<p>
					Each release publishes glibc and musl archives. Verify the download with its <code>.sha256</code> file and
					<code>gh attestation verify</code>, unpack the daemon archive and run its installer.
				</p>
				<div class="card-foot">
					<a class="text-link" href={site.releasesUrl}>Releases</a>
				</div>
			</article>
			<article class="card">
				<h3>macOS (Apple Silicon)</h3>
				<p>
					macOS 14 or newer, tested on macOS 15. Install from the tap, then install the login service.
				</p>
				<CopyBox title="macOS" text={`${site.homebrewInstall}\npohunek service install`} />
			</article>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="container section">
		<p>
			The full procedure, including archive verification, the login service, upgrades and runtime packages, is in the
			<a class="text-link" href="/docs/install/">install guide</a>.
		</p>
	</section>
</MarketingLayout>

<style>
	.note {
		margin-top: 1rem;
	}
</style>
